# Voice over masters, archived 2026-08-31 to r2://brock-masters/fleetcommand/vo/
# and verified by a byte for byte readback. Raw takes are COLD tier per
# MEDIA-POLICY: the archive holds them, the repo never does. assets/MASTERS.md
# names every object. Same handling as doctrine's host frames.
assets/vo/

# A SECOND, DIFFERENT SET OF VOICE TAKES, and the distinction is the whole
# point of this block. The R2 archive above holds three .webm files taken out
# of ~/Downloads. These are 9 .wav and .mp3 takes in submission/vo/, about
# 62MB, and NOTHING archived them: the line above ignores assets/vo/, a folder
# that does not exist on this disk, so it protected a phantom while the real
# files sat untracked AND unignored, one sweeping `git add -A` from history.
# Do not read MASTERS.md as covering these. Per submission/vo/NOTES.md they are
# references rather than keepers (recorded through the convicted XLR cable), so
# they are ignored rather than archived, and whether they are worth a COLD tier
# object at all is Brock's call. NOTES.md itself stays tracked: it carries the
# paused session state, the mic gain setting, and the note that the film is
# missing from disk.
submission/vo/*.wav
submission/vo/*.mp3

# The two narrator renders mix8.mjs writes. Generated media beside the film
# that is already ignored above, same rule: the pipeline is tracked, its
# output never is. They used to be written to a Desktop on another Mac, which
# is why they were never in anyone's way before.
submission/fleetcommand-NARRATOR-clean.mp4
submission/fleetcommand-NARRATOR-music.mp4

# VO session media: reference takes, too big for git. NOTES.md IS tracked.
submission/vo/*.wav
submission/vo/*.mp3
